-- title:
--   Inverse image ideal sheaf on affine opens is the extended ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes, let $I$ be an element of `X.IdealSheafData`, that is, a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on $X$ recorded by the data of an ideal $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U \subseteq \Gamma(U,\mathcal O_X)$ for every affine open $U$ of $X$, compatible under localisation, and let $f \colon Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $U$ be an affine open of $X$ and $V$ an affine open of $Y$ with $V \le f^{-1}(U)$, this containment being the hypothesis `hVU`. Then the section of the comap ideal sheaf `I.comap f` over $V$ — the ideal sheaf of the closed immersion into $Y$ obtained by pulling back along $f$ the closed subscheme of $X$ cut out by $I$, i.e. the kernel of the first projection from the fibre product of $f$ and the inclusion of that subscheme — coincides with the image ideal $(I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U)\cdot\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_Y)$, namely the ideal of $\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_Y)$ generated by the image of $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ under the ring map $\Gamma(U,\mathcal O_X) \to \Gamma(V,\mathcal O_Y)$ given by `f.appLE U V hVU`, the map induced by $f$ on sections relative to the containment $V \le f^{-1}(U)$.
--
--   This is the affine-local description of the scheme-theoretic inverse image of a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf: on an affine open $V$ of $Y$ mapping into an affine open $U$ of $X$, the pulled-back ideal sheaf is generated by the image of the ideal over $U$. It extends the case of an open immersion available in Mathlib to arbitrary morphisms with no affineness assumption on $f$, and is used in the construction and computation of ideal sheaves on projective space and in the relative Picard group development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_ideal_comap_of_le.lean

import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Functorial

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

theorem AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_le
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData) (f : Y ⟶ X) (U : X.affineOpens)
    (V : Y.affineOpens) (hVU : (V : Y.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens)) :
    (I.comap f).ideal V = (I.ideal U).map (f.appLE U V hVU).hom := by sorry
